diff --git a/docs/ref/class-based-views/base.txt b/docs/ref/class-based-views/base.txt
index 4c1d0e12b5..091cc5ac3a 100644
--- a/docs/ref/class-based-views/base.txt
+++ b/docs/ref/class-based-views/base.txt
@@ -1,3 +0,0 @@
-==========
-Base views
-==========
@@ -5,5 +1,0 @@ Base views
-The following three classes provide much of the functionality needed to create
-Django views. You may think of them as *parent* views, which can be used by
-themselves or inherited from. They may not provide all the capabilities
-required for projects, in which case there are Mixins and Generic class-based
-views.
@@ -11,4 +2,0 @@ views.
-Many of Django's built-in class-based views inherit from other class-based
-views or various mixins. Because this inheritance chain is very important, the
-ancestor classes are  documented under the section title of **Ancestors (MRO)**.
-MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
@@ -16,2 +3,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-``View``
-========
@@ -19 +4,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-.. class:: django.views.generic.base.View
@@ -21,3 +5,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-    The master class-based base view. All other class-based views inherit from
-    this base class. It isn't strictly a generic view and thus can also be
-    imported from ``django.views``.
@@ -25 +6,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-    **Method Flowchart**
@@ -27,4 +7,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-    #. :meth:`setup()`
-    #. :meth:`dispatch()`
-    #. :meth:`http_method_not_allowed()`
-    #. :meth:`options()`
@@ -32 +8,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-    **Example views.py**::
@@ -34,2 +9,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-        from django.http import HttpResponse
-        from django.views import View
@@ -37 +10,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-        class MyView(View):
@@ -39,2 +11,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-            def get(self, request, *args, **kwargs):
-                return HttpResponse('Hello, World!')
@@ -42 +12,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-    **Example urls.py**::
@@ -44 +13,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-        from django.urls import path
@@ -46 +14,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-        from myapp.views import MyView
@@ -48,3 +15,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-        urlpatterns = [
-            path('mine/', MyView.as_view(), name='my-view'),
-        ]
@@ -52 +16,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
-    **Attributes**
@@ -54 +17,0 @@ MRO is an acronym for Method Resolution Order.
