-Creating forms from models
-==========================
@@ -5 +1,0 @@ Creating forms from models
-.. currentmodule:: django.forms
@@ -7,3 +2,0 @@ Creating forms from models
-``ModelForm``
-=============
-.. class:: ModelForm
@@ -11,5 +3,0 @@ Creating forms from models
-If you're building a database-driven app, chances are you'll have forms that
-map closely to Django models. For instance, you might have a ``BlogComment``
-model, and you want to create a form that lets people submit comments. In this
-case, it would be redundant to define the field types in your form, because
-you've already defined the fields in your model.
@@ -17,2 +4,0 @@ you've already defined the fields in your model.
-For this reason, Django provides a helper class that lets you create a ``Form``
-class from a Django model.
@@ -20 +5,0 @@ class from a Django model.
-For example::
@@ -22,2 +6,0 @@ For example::
-    >>> from django.forms import ModelForm
-    >>> from myapp.models import Article
@@ -25,5 +7,0 @@ For example::
-    # Create the form class.
-    >>> class ArticleForm(ModelForm):
-    ...     class Meta:
-    ...         model = Article
-    ...         fields = ['pub_date', 'headline', 'content', 'reporter']
@@ -31,2 +8,0 @@ For example::
-    # Creating a form to add an article.
-    >>> form = ArticleForm()
@@ -34,3 +9,0 @@ For example::
-    # Creating a form to change an existing article.
-    >>> article = Article.objects.get(pk=1)
-    >>> form = ArticleForm(instance=article)
@@ -38,2 +10,0 @@ For example::
-Field types
